/-! # Normally flat initial equations lift with maximal-ideal coefficients

Source: Hironaka, Certain numerical characters of singularities (1970),
proof of Lemma 20, (20.6) and the coefficient lifting before (20.7), p.179.
(blueprint: lem-trf-normal-flat-initial-coefficient-lifting).
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace Hironaka

/-- The coefficient-lifting assertion before Hironaka (1970), (20.7), p.179.
(blueprint: lem-trf-normal-flat-initial-coefficient-lifting).

The parameter map is fixed on coefficients and every variable by `IsParameterGradedMap`.
The constructed `adicInitialIdeal` is the tangent graded quotient's kernel: in degree
`e` this is precisely the classes of elements of `b ∩ M^e`. The double quotient in
`hflat` is canonically `T/P`, retaining the published associated-graded scalar action.
The initial form of `f i` is its class in `M^(d i)/M^(d i + 1)`, placed in
degree `d i` of `gr_M T`. No reducedness is assumed, and the degrees need not be
ordered. The coefficients at inactive indices are unrestricted and do not enter the sum.

Proof, following the six steps of the node:
1. The regular-parameter theorem makes the x-prefix regular and `A = T/P` regular
local. The regular-sequence graded-polynomial theorem identifies `H = gr_P T`
with `A[X]`. The quotient maps `H` onto `G = gr_I (T/b)` degreewise; write its
kernel as `K_e` and the P-initial classes of the equations as `F_i`.
2. Each `G_e` is flat as a direct summand of the flat graded sum. The flat-quotient
tensor-injectivity theorem applied with the residue field identifies `K_e/nK_e`
with the fibre kernel and gives `K_e ∩ nH_e = nK_e`, where `n = M/P`.
3. The normal-flat double-initial-ideal lemma identifies the tangent kernel with
the extension of the fibre kernel to `k[X,Y]`. Evaluating `Y = 0` shows that the
`φ_i` generate the fibre kernel. Expansion in x-monomials shows that reduction
of `F_i` modulo `n` is exactly `φ_i`.
4. The finite degree-e monomial basis of `H_e` and Noetherianity make `K_e`
finite. Its residue quotient is generated by the degree-e monomial multiples
of the `φ_i`. Degreewise Nakayama therefore gives
`K_e = Σ_(d_i ≤ e) H_(e-d_i) F_i`.
5. Expand `u` in degree-n x-monomials. Since `u ∈ M^(n+1)`, independence of
those monomials in `gr_M T = k[X,Y]` puts every coefficient in `M`. Thus its
P-initial class `U` lies in `nH_n ∩ K_n = nK_n`.
6. Distribute `n` over the generators from step 4 and lift the finitely many
coefficients from `n` to `M`. Evaluating the x-monomials gives coefficients
in `M P^(n-d_i)` and the asserted remainder in `P^(n+1)`. The remainder is
also in `b`, since `u` and every `f_i` are in `b`. If the index set is empty,
`K_n = 0` gives the same result, including `n = 0`.
-/
theorem normalFlatInitialCoefficientLifting
    {T : Type u} [CommRing T] [IsRegularLocalRing T]
    (r s : ℕ) (x : Fin (r + 1) → T) (y : Fin s → T)
    (hparams : IsLocalRing.IsRegularSystemOfParameters (List.ofFn x ++ List.ofFn y))
    (b : Ideal T) (hb : b ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (hflat : Module.Flat
      ((T ⧸ b) ⧸ (Ideal.span (Set.range x)).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk b))
      (Ideal.associatedGraded ((Ideal.span (Set.range x)).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk b))))
    (χ : MvPolynomial (Fin (r + 1) ⊕ Fin s) (IsLocalRing.ResidueField T) →+*
      Ideal.associatedGraded (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T))
    (hχ : IsParameterGradedMap x y χ)
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 ≤ m) (f : Fin m → T) (d : Fin m → ℕ)
    (φ : Fin m → MvPolynomial (Fin (r + 1)) (IsLocalRing.ResidueField T))
    (hdpos : ∀ i, 1 ≤ d i)
    (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ b ∧ f i ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range x) ^ d i ∧
      adicOrder (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T) (f i) = d i)
    (hφ : ∀ i, (φ i).IsHomogeneous (d i) ∧
      ∃ hi : f i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T ^ d i,
        χ (MvPolynomial.rename Sum.inl (φ i)) =
          DirectSum.of (Ideal.associatedGradedPiece (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T)) (d i)
            (Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨f i, hi⟩))
    (hbasis : IsMinimalGeneratingFamily
      (adicInitialIdeal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T) b)
      (fun i ↦ χ (MvPolynomial.rename Sum.inl (φ i))))
    (n : ℕ) (u : T) (hu : u ∈ b ⊓ Ideal.span (Set.range x) ^ n ⊓
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T ^ (n + 1)) :
    ∃ c : Fin m → T,
      (∀ i, d i ≤ n → c i ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T * Ideal.span (Set.range x) ^ (n - d i)) ∧
      u - ∑ i ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun i ↦ d i ≤ n), c i * f i ∈
        b ⊓ Ideal.span (Set.range x) ^ (n + 1) := by
  sorry

end Hironaka
